---

The MIT License above covers the code in this repository.

It does not and cannot change the licences of the third-party packages the app
depends on, which are listed in requirements.txt and keep their own terms. All
of them are permissive except one:

  pyfamsa (a wrapper around FAMSA, used for the multiple sequence alignment)
  is GPL-3.0-or-later.

So while this repository's own code is MIT and may be reused freely, anyone who
redistributes the application as a whole, with the alignment feature in place,
has to honour GPL-3.0 for that component. The alignment is the only feature
that depends on it, and vhh_core.build_alignment is the only place it is
imported, so a derivative work that does not need FAMSA can drop the dependency
and is then unencumbered by it.

This note is a statement of what the dependency licences say, not legal advice.

---

Two bundled data files are not MIT either, and keep the terms they came with:

  data/sabdab/        a snapshot of SAbDab2's single-domain entries, from the
                      Oxford Protein Informatics Group, under CC-BY 4.0. See
                      data/sabdab/LICENSE. Redistribution is permitted with
                      attribution, which is what that file and the app's own
                      screen provide.

  data/ecoli_codon_usage.csv
                      E. coli codon usage from the Kazusa database, under
                      CC0-1.0, a public-domain dedication.

Neither affects the licence of the code.
